xkIHsRpfLDOsUjAL8Wj9vWDOAGuKgK2HsGkUeJWNKq7umWQuyhSVoVRl71SkCKytucQqcHIuaQme6J0kO5oPhVXMhhatsEoUyBCTX2YcxnJPgqgAvHm9Qxe4x5MVHXYNfYIKm0M1VPd9RcuAu1ymnGxLpcMpdYpwy_N1cjIJAswvxb3w96gTSQi11BloFHsFpJ2X45Qc3vuW6w3tU3ExjF4qGr_W4pOosuJeurHqBMzcBMrZ6rHFdgxUjed2-MlXeKbfpDkhpSoZpfPGHCbHL_9d6eRfr5KmZ2sJgr1-7kfj8GS9PzjOsrfmUU9CZlfm-MRPu9vEbBwBqd9dzIDoQtknUVLvsYRoG50GecvZf2i1g6MgVN_lu_GKc7\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"### Overview\n`src/labels.js` maps a score to one of three labels.\n\n### How It Works\n`labelFor(score)` checks thresholds in descending order:\n- `score >= 80` → `\"strong\"`\n- `score >= 50` → `\"developing\"`\n- Otherwise → `\"starting\"`\n\nBoth thresholds are inclusive.\n\n### Gotchas\nValues that don’t satisfy either comparison—including `NaN`—return `\"starting\"`. JavaScript comparison coercion applies to non-number inputs.\n\n### Where Things Live\nThe mapping is implemented entirely in `src/labels.js`.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_037fdb3e8219424d016ab60304fd0887d0afdbd23dc04fcff5\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","usage":{"input":783,"output":241,"cacheRead":1536,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":117,"totalTokens":2560,"cost":{"input":0.0000783,"output":0.00012049999999999999,"cacheRead":0.000015360000000000002,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00021416000000000002}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1790313215763,"responseId":"resp_037fdb3e8219424d016ab603000d8887d09333c998044527cf","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
